from 1993 to 2000 boy meets world was a  tgif  staple the show shared a friday prime  time block with kid-friendly sitcoms  family matters and step by step  when those two shows moved on boy meets  world endured sitting comfortably  alongside sabrina the teenage witch and  various other shows for the friday  primetime blog  on boy meets world writer strong played  corey's best friend sean hunter  in contrast to corey's idyllic life  shawn's storylines often had the  teenager grapple with some serious life  issues  he was abandoned by his stepmother  several times and he lost his father  soon after they reunited for starters  it was all the things that you taught me  that made me wonder if it was the right  place for me or not  but you didn't teach me enough after boy  meets world wrapped the world saw less  and less of strong  he disappeared from television sets for  years until he reprised the role of sean  all grown up for girl meets world years  later strong opened up about why his  presence became scarce  it turns out the same storylines that  made him memorable have something to do  with the reason why hollywood seemingly  won't cast him anymore  in an interview with vice the actor  admitted that his desire to be  considered a serious professional  clouded his judgment during his time on  boy meets world as an adult he now  recognizes his aloofness  i wanted to be a poet and academic  writer there was definitely a period  where i thought i was way cooler than  boy meets world  as a result the writers wrote more  dramatic storylines to keep the teenage  strong  interested in his role regardless of  their efforts he was still miserable  he didn't enjoy living up to the  expectations that came along with fame  he recalled one instance when he  participated in a sale with the stars  charity cruise that left him scarred  regarding the fans on the boat strong  told vice they want a certain version of  you  whether that's sean hunter or this  perfect teen idol boyfriend and suddenly  you have to be that person 24 hours a  day  strong nearly quit boy meets world soon  after but finished the show's run with  the support of his parents  after boy meets world ended strong  enrolled at columbia university per his  website  according to mental flaws his famous  classmates included anna paquin  julia stiles and joseph gordon-levitt  their feature film stardom meant he  received less attention from the media  while in school  which he preferred during his studies  strong stayed away from hollywood  only taking one semester off to film the  indie horror hit  cabin fever  he continued his education after  colombia and earned an mfa in fiction  and literature from bennington college  afterwards strong returned to work in  the entertainment industry  instead of television roles he took on  more horror films including 2017's  borderland pulse 3 and captain fever 2  spring fever finding that he preferred  to remain behind the camera  strong also began co-directing short  films with his brother in between  projects he also lends his voice to  narrate audiobooks  since his reprisal of sean hunter on  girl meets world strong has added voice  over work to his list of credits  including the disney animated shows  mighty magiswords and star vs the forces  of evil  the next gen spin-off girl meets world  saw the return of writer strong to  network television  although he was reluctant to return he  said he was able to find a compromise  with the show  i knew that playing sean again was going  to be the final nail in the coffin of  ever doing anything else as an actor so  i did a trade  strong originally asked for seven  episodes but ended up directing  18 of them for the show which ran for  three seasons  former co-stars ben savage also directed  a handful of girl meets world episodes  bringing the history of the show full  circle strong is now a husband and a  father he married actress alexandra  barreto in 2013  and they have one son check out one of  our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite childhood stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

